Z||000006||Black88GT||03-21-2001||08:57 PM||||Some of you guys need to calm down a bit.  The first line stated he found it on a car club email group.  I have been screwed over by Thrifty on my last vacation so it doesn't break my heart one bit.  And how would they prove it anyway?  Are they going to tear down the motor and examine every part?  I guess they could try a compression test but they would have to have proof of the compression before those guys got a hold of it.  In other words, it would be too much of their time and money for a 6,000 car.  Add lawyer fee's on top of the mechanics labor costs and you could buy another Neon.  I guess arguing this is silly so I don't know why I am bothering||||reg||1
